y/bg/\",\"title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is\"},{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/\",\"title\":\"Chapter Eight: Attaining the Supreme\"}],\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/2/\",\"bb\":2092,\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"pager\":{\"previous\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/1/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 1\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]},\"next\":{\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/3/\",\"title\":\"TEXT 3\",\"has_advanced_view\":false,\"translations\":[\"en\",\"cs\",\"es\",\"bg\",\"pt-br\",\"ru\",\"sk\",\"hr\",\"pl\",\"da\",\"de\",\"et\",\"fr\",\"hu\",\"ko\",\"lt\",\"nl\",\"sl\",\"uk\",\"ja\"]}},\"child_items\":[{\"section\":\"devanagari\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.devanagari\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.DevanagariRecord\",\"title\":\"devanagari\",\"id\":2359,\"bb\":568181,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/2/devanagari/\",\"body_final\":\"अधियज्ञ: कथं कोऽत्र देहेऽस्मिन्मधुसूदन ।
प्रयाणकाले च कथं ज्ञेयोऽसि नियतात्मभि: ॥ २ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2360,\"bb\":2093,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/2/b2093/\",\"body_value\":\"adhiyajñaḥ kathaṁ ko ’tra
dehe ’smin madhusūdana
prayāṇa-kāle ca kathaṁ
jñeyo ’si niyatātmabhiḥ\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":2361,\"bb\":2094,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/2/b2094/\",\"shadow_value\":\"adhiyajñaḥ – the Lord of sacrifice; katham – how; kaḥ – who; atra – here; dehe – in the body; asmin – this; madhusūdana – O Madhusūdana; prayāṇa-kāle – at the time of death; ca – and; katham – how; jñeyaḥ asi – You can be known; niyata-ātmabhiḥ – by the self-controlled.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"adhiyajñaḥ\",\"translation\":\"the Lord of sacrifice\"},{\"word\":\"katham\",\"translation\":\"how\"},{\"word\":\"kaḥ\",\"translation\":\"who\"},{\"word\":\"atra\",\"translation\":\"here\"},{\"word\":\"dehe\",\"translation\":\"in the body\"},{\"word\":\"asmin\",\"translation\":\"this\"},{\"word\":\"madhusūdana\",\"translation\":\"O Madhusūdana\"},{\"word\":\"prayāṇa-kāle\",\"translation\":\"at the time of death\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"and\"},{\"word\":\"katham\",\"translation\":\"how\"},{\"word\":\"jñeyaḥ asi\",\"translation\":\"You can be known\"},{\"word\":\"niyata-ātmabhiḥ\",\"translation\":\"by the self-controlled\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":2362,\"bb\":2095,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/2/b2095/\",\"body_value\":\"Who is the Lord of sacrifice, and how does He live in the body, O Madhusūdana? And how can those engaged in devotional service know You at the time of death?\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2363,\"bb\":2096,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/2/b2096/\",\"body_value\":\"“Lord of sacrifice” may refer to either Indra or Viṣṇu. Viṣṇu is the chief of the primal demigods, including Brahmā and Śiva, and Indra is the chief of the administrative demigods. Both Indra and Viṣṇu are worshiped by yajña performances. But here Arjuna asks who is actually the Lord of yajña (sacrifice) and how the Lord is residing within the body of the living entity.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2364,\"bb\":2097,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/2/b2097/\",\"body_value\":\"Arjuna addresses the Lord as Madhusūdana because Kṛṣṇa once killed a demon named Madhu. Actually these questions, which are of the nature of doubts, should not have arisen in the mind of Arjuna, because Arjuna is a Kṛṣṇa conscious devotee. Therefore these doubts are like demons. Since Kṛṣṇa is so expert in killing demons, Arjuna here addresses Him as Madhusūdana so that Kṛṣṇa might kill the demonic doubts that arise in Arjuna’s mind.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2365,\"bb\":2098,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/8/2/b2098/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 8.2\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 8.2\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n30:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n26:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-4 w-full max-w-screen-xl mx-au